1. CONCEPT A: EDITORIAL LUXURY ('The Gastronomic Atelier') =E2=80=94 RECOMMEN=
DED
- Visual Character: High-fashion culinary monograph, old-world Levantine gran=
deur.
- Typography: Playfair Display (dramatic transitional serif) paired with Plus=
 Jakarta Sans and classical Amiri Arabic script.
- Composition: Asymmetric 16:10 feature spreads for signature dishes, clean h=
orizontal rows separated by 1px hairlines, and dotted bistro tables for mezze=
. Zero repetitive cards.
- Ordering UX: Slide-over order drawer on desktop, floating bottom pill on mo=
bile, single-column requisition slip checkout, and perforated printed ticket =
confirmation.

2. CONCEPT B: MINIMAL FINE DINING ('Swiss Precision & Haute Cuisine')
- Visual Character: Modernist Bauhaus restraint, 3-Michelin-star tasting menu=
 clarity.
- Typography: Inter paired with Space Grotesk (tabular numerals throughout).
- Composition: Tabular data matrix. Continuous 1px hairline rules. Strict 0px=
 corner radius across all elements (buttons, image frames, inputs, modals).
- Ordering UX: Sticky left-hand navigation rail on desktop, inline numeric st=
eppers directly in table rows, and structured data checkout matrix.

3. CONCEPT C: MODERN HIGH-CONTRAST HOSPITALITY ('The Dark & Stark')
- Visual Character: Nocturnal Beirut haute hospitality inspired by oak lump c=
harcoal, white heat, smoke, and black basalt stone.
- Typography: Monumental Syne display headings (up to 64px) paired with sharp=
 Space Grotesk.
- Composition: Pitch-black canvas (#000000) with chiaroscuro food photography=
 emerging from darkness. Signature dishes feature dramatic high-contrast whit=
e inversion bursts.
- Ordering UX: Luminous floating cart capsule, solid white action blocks that=
 invert to outlines on hover, and live order tracking screen.

